{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787341831527,"sessionID":"ses_fda202bcdffec9r6rZINkUTph5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_e32fc70052f64379bdbafe9d","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/cyr/kernel/MEMORY.md"},"output":"<path>/home/cyr/kernel/MEMORY.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # MEMORY.md — kernel project state\n2: \n3: Read this first. Source of truth when context is compacted.\n4: The full phase-by-phase plan lives in `AGENTS.md` — this file is state,\n5: decisions, and gotchas. Update at milestones or near context limits.\n6: \n7: ## Status (as of 2026-08-22)\n8: \n9: **Planning converged; coding starts next session at Phase 0.**\n10: No code has changed yet (docs only: AGENTS.md, MEMORY.md, opencode.json,\n11: scripts/overnight.sh). Unattended runs: `scripts/overnight.sh` drives\n12: `opencode run --auto --continue` in rounds; stop with `touch .overnight-stop`;\n13: progress in `.overnight.log`. First actions: Phase 0 (`git init`, commit tree\n14: verbatim), then Phase 1 per AGENTS.md.\n15: \n16: ## Project vision (endgame, user's words)\n17: \n18: System programming in **Go**, on a deliberately **non-POSIX** capability\n19: microkernel — \"otherwise it's replicating Linux, which is going for Rust\n20: and C.\" Portable by construction to x86_64 / aarch64 / riscv64: services are\n21: `.wasm` bytecode and never get ported; only the thin substrate shell does.\n22: \n23: ## Decision history (why the repo looks like this)\n24: \n25: 1. **Original vision**: microkernel *is* an 8-opcode restricted ISA machine\n26:    (`kernel/vm/isa.h`, interpreter in C) for portability/minimal TCB.\n27: 2. **The pivot (rejected)**: a prior agent was asked to use Plan 9 asm\n28:    instead of GNU as, escalated into porting the full Go runtime to bare\n29:    metal: custom GOOS=baremetal, 13 GOROOT patches ($GOROOT_BARE), merged\n30:    PE shim+Go image. User calls this \"a nightmare\" — it buried the 8-opcode\n31:    kernel under a runtime port nobody asked for. Artifacts still in tree:\n32:    `gokernel/`, `tools/goshim/`, Go rules in Makefile, marker handoff in\n33:    `kernel/main.c`. All retired in Phases 2–3.\n34: 3. **Converged design**: wasm + mini-WASI as guest ABI (replaces the\n35:    8-opcode ISA entirely once wasm works). Rationale: stock toolchains\n36:    (Go wasip1 since 1.21 — zero patching, the anti-nightmare), sandboxing,\n37:    byte-identical portability. 8-opcode ISA proved native boot in Phase 1,\n38:    then retired to git history.\n39: \n40: User-approved choices: retire 8-opcode ISA · adapt wasm3 (MIT, not WAMR,\n41: not clean-room) · guest ladder C→Rust→Go · GNU as (Plan 9 asm mandate dead)\n42: · freestanding C++20 with RAII allowed · separate servers over message ports\n43: (NOT a stacked monolith) · multiuser = policy layer via login.wasm capability\n44: grants, not ABI-baked.\n45: \n46: ## Architecture decisions (binding)\n47: \n48: - Sessions = wasm instances; isolation via engine bounds checks, NOT MMU.\n49: - WASI is per-session capability surface implemented by the kernel natively;\n50:   there is no \"WASI server\". FS/login/drivers-policy are separate .wasm\n51:   servers talking over kernel-relayed message ports (Phase 4 imports).\n52: - Drivers: raw HW only in tiny frozen native device-window shims inside the\n53:   substrate; wasm holds policy. New hardware class ⇒ substrate edit.\n54: - Client→FS routing decision deferred to Phase 5: kernel-routed preview1\n55:   path ops vs client lib over ports. Document choice here when made.\n56: - No fork/exec/signals/global namespace ever. Non-POSIX is the point.\n57: \n58: ## What survives / what gets retired\n59: \n60: Survives: UEFI C shim core (`kernel/{main,serial,cpu,mm,gdt_idt,lib,loader}`,\n61: link.ld), mkpefi.py approach, mtools disk flow, make-test harness pattern,\n62: `tools/vasm` until Phase 5 cleanup.\n63: Retired (recoverable from Phase-0 git snapshot): `gokernel/*`,\n64: `tools/goshim/*` (Plan 9 asm IDT bank), `scripts/goaddr.sh`, all\n65: GOROOT_BARE make rules, GO_MAGIC markers in main.c, eventually\n66: `kernel/vm/ tools/vasm programs/demo.*`.\n67: \n68: ## Environment (no root!)\n69: \n70: - `~/.local/osdev-root`: qemu-system-x86_64 10.x, OVMF_CODE_4M/VARS_4M.fd,\n71:   mtools, seabios. QEMU needs `LD_LIBRARY_PATH=$ROOT/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu`\n72:   and `-L $ROOT/usr/share/qemu -L $ROOT/usr/share/seabios`.\n73: - Network OK; downloads/install prefixes under `~/.local` work (uid 1000).\n74: - System go exists (check version ≥1.21 for wasip1). $GOROOT_BARE is DEAD —\n75:   never reference or rebuild it; do not delete it either (out of repo scope).\n76: - KVM available iff /dev/kvm writable, else TCG `-accel tcg` (fine).\n77: \n78: ## Gotchas (still valid — don't relearn)\n79: \n80: - PE32+ optional header offsets above CheckSum are easy to get wrong;\n81:   section table entries exactly 40 bytes. mkpefi.py encodes these — touch\n82:   carefully.\n83: - objcopy cannot emit EFI PEs here; mkpefi.py is the ELF→PE converter and\n84:   must parse PT_LOAD itself (objcopy -O binary start-vaddr bug).\n85: - OVMF rejects images whose DOS stub isn't padded to exactly 0x80 before\n86:   'PE\\0\\0' → falls to UEFI shell (\"Unsupported\").\n87: - Loader uses raw vtable offsets into EFI protocols (`(char*)sfs+8`,\n88:   `file+56` etc.) — spec-fixed but fragile; keep FW1..FW5 wrappers.\n89: - Serial log greps: strip ANSI escapes before matching.\n90: - Stale-object danger: after changing kernel sources, rebuild clean; a boot\n91:   log older than its binary is worthless (this bit during the Go era).\n92: - QEMU TCG supports AVX2 with `-cpu max`; irrelevant post-ISA-retirement.\n93: \n94: ## Obsolete knowledge (historical — gone with the Go pivot)\n95: \n96: GOROOT_BARE rebuild procedure, go-tool-asm quirks (DATA $sym(SB), bare\n97: INB/OUTB, nosplit self-JMP), linkname/cgo_import_static linker restrictions,\n98: baremetal GOOS patch list, pageAlloc 32-bit-style workaround, doubled serial\n99: chars issue. Do not resurrect; kept here only so future agents don't dig.\n100: \n101: ## Next actions (verbatim checklist for next session)\n102: \n103: 1. `git init && printf 'build/\\n' > .gitignore && git add -A && git commit`\n104:    — verbatim snapshot BEFORE any surgery.\n105: 2. Phase 1 per AGENTS.md: rewire main.c → kmain(); Makefile objects;\n106:    mkpefi shim-only; root-cause loader regression (stale log vs\n107:    LocateProtocol); gate = KERNEL-OK + out 0x28 + 'E'.\n108: 3. Proceed Phase 2 onward only while gates stay green.\n\n(End of file - total 108 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# MEMORY.md — kernel project state\n\nRead this first. Source of truth when context is compacted.\nThe full phase-by-phase plan lives in `AGENTS.md` — this file is state,\ndecisions, and gotchas. Update at milestones or near context limits.\n\n## Status (as of 2026-08-22)\n\n**Planning converged; coding starts next session at Phase 0.**\nNo code has changed yet (docs only: AGENTS.md, MEMORY.md, opencode.json,\nscripts/overnight.sh). Unattended runs: `scripts/overnight.sh` drives\n`opencode run --auto --continue` in rounds; stop with `touch .overnight-stop`;\nprogress in `.overnight.log`. First actions: Phase 0 (`git init`, commit tree\nverbatim), then Phase 1 per AGENTS.md.\n\n## Project vision (endgame, user's words)\n\nSystem programming in **Go**, on a deliberately **non-POSIX** capability\nmicrokernel — \"otherwise it's replicating Linux, which is going for Rust\nand C.\" Portable by construction to x86_64 / aarch64 / riscv64: services are","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/cyr/kernel/MEMORY.md","text":"# MEMORY.md — kernel project state\n\nRead this first. Source of truth when context is compacted.\nThe full phase-by-phase plan lives in `AGENTS.md` — this file is state,\ndecisions, and gotchas. Update at milestones or near context limits.\n\n## Status (as of 2026-08-22)\n\n**Planning converged; coding starts next session at Phase 0.**\nNo code has changed yet (docs only: AGENTS.md, MEMORY.md, opencode.json,\nscripts/overnight.sh). Unattended runs: `scripts/overnight.sh` drives\n`opencode run --auto --continue` in rounds; stop with `touch .overnight-stop`;\nprogress in `.overnight.log`. First actions: Phase 0 (`git init`, commit tree\nverbatim), then Phase 1 per AGENTS.md.\n\n## Project vision (endgame, user's words)\n\nSystem programming in **Go**, on a deliberately **non-POSIX** capability\nmicrokernel — \"otherwise it's replicating Linux, which is going for Rust\nand C.\" Portable by construction to x86_64 / aarch64 / riscv64: services are\n`.wasm` bytecode and never get ported; only the thin substrate shell does.\n\n## Decision history (why the repo looks like this)\n\n1. **Original vision**: microkernel *is* an 8-opcode restricted ISA machine\n   (`kernel/vm/isa.h`, interpreter in C) for portability/minimal TCB.\n2. **The pivot (rejected)**: a prior agent was asked to use Plan 9 asm\n   instead of GNU as, escalated into porting the full Go runtime to bare\n   metal: custom GOOS=baremetal, 13 GOROOT patches ($GOROOT_BARE), merged\n   PE shim+Go image. User calls this \"a nightmare\" — it buried the 8-opcode\n   kernel under a runtime port nobody asked for. Artifacts still in tree:\n   `gokernel/`, `tools/goshim/`, Go rules in Makefile, marker handoff in\n   `kernel/main.c`. All retired in Phases 2–3.\n3. **Converged design**: wasm + mini-WASI as guest ABI (replaces the\n   8-opcode ISA entirely once wasm works). Rationale: stock toolchains\n   (Go wasip1 since 1.21 — zero patching, the anti-nightmare), sandboxing,\n   byte-identical portability. 8-opcode ISA proved native boot in Phase 1,\n   then retired to git history.\n\nUser-approved choices: retire 8-opcode ISA · adapt wasm3 (MIT, not WAMR,\nnot clean-room) · guest ladder C→Rust→Go · GNU as (Plan 9 asm mandate dead)\n· freestanding C++20 with RAII allowed · separate servers over message ports\n(NOT a stacked monolith) · multiuser = policy layer via login.wasm capability\ngrants, not ABI-baked.\n\n## Architecture decisions (binding)\n\n- Sessions = wasm instances; isolation via engine bounds checks, NOT MMU.\n- WASI is per-session capability surface implemented by the kernel natively;\n  there is no \"WASI server\". FS/login/drivers-policy are separate .wasm\n  servers talking over kernel-relayed message ports (Phase 4 imports).\n- Drivers: raw HW only in tiny frozen native device-window shims inside the\n  substrate; wasm holds policy. New hardware class ⇒ substrate edit.\n- Client→FS routing decision deferred to Phase 5: kernel-routed preview1\n  path ops vs client lib over ports. Document choice here when made.\n- No fork/exec/signals/global namespace ever. Non-POSIX is the point.\n\n## What survives / what gets retired\n\nSurvives: UEFI C shim core (`kernel/{main,serial,cpu,mm,gdt_idt,lib,loader}`,\nlink.ld), mkpefi.py approach, mtools disk flow, make-test harness pattern,\n`tools/vasm` until Phase 5 cleanup.\nRetired (recoverable from Phase-0 git snapshot): `gokernel/*`,\n`tools/goshim/*` (Plan 9 asm IDT bank), `scripts/goaddr.sh`, all\nGOROOT_BARE make rules, GO_MAGIC markers in main.c, eventually\n`kernel/vm/ tools/vasm programs/demo.*`.\n\n## Environment (no root!)\n\n- `~/.local/osdev-root`: qemu-system-x86_64 10.x, OVMF_CODE_4M/VARS_4M.fd,\n  mtools, seabios. QEMU needs `LD_LIBRARY_PATH=$ROOT/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu`\n  and `-L $ROOT/usr/share/qemu -L $ROOT/usr/share/seabios`.\n- Network OK; downloads/install prefixes under `~/.local` work (uid 1000).\n- System go exists (check version ≥1.21 for wasip1). $GOROOT_BARE is DEAD —\n  never reference or rebuild it; do not delete it either (out of repo scope).\n- KVM available iff /dev/kvm writable, else TCG `-accel tcg` (fine).\n\n## Gotchas (still valid — don't relearn)\n\n- PE32+ optional header offsets above CheckSum are easy to get wrong;\n  section table entries exactly 40 bytes. mkpefi.py encodes these — touch\n  carefully.\n- objcopy cannot emit EFI PEs here; mkpefi.py is the ELF→PE converter and\n  must parse PT_LOAD itself (objcopy -O binary start-vaddr bug).\n- OVMF rejects images whose DOS stub isn't padded to exactly 0x80 before\n  'PE\\0\\0' → falls to UEFI shell (\"Unsupported\").\n- Loader uses raw vtable offsets into EFI protocols (`(char*)sfs+8`,\n  `file+56` etc.) — spec-fixed but fragile; keep FW1..FW5 wrappers.\n- Serial log greps: strip ANSI escapes before matching.\n- Stale-object danger: after changing kernel sources, rebuild clean; a boot\n  log older than its binary is worthless (this bit during the Go era).\n- QEMU TCG supports AVX2 with `-cpu max`; irrelevant post-ISA-retirement.\n\n## Obsolete knowledge (historical — gone with the Go pivot)\n\nGOROOT_BARE rebuild procedure, go-tool-asm quirks (DATA $sym(SB), bare\nINB/OUTB, nosplit self-JMP), linkname/cgo_import_static linker restrictions,\nbaremetal GOOS patch list, pageAlloc 32-bit-style workaround, doubled serial\nchars issue. Do not resurrect; kept here only so future agents don't dig.\n\n## Next actions (verbatim checklist for next session)\n\n1. `git init && printf 'build/\\n' > .gitignore && git add -A && git commit`\n   — verbatim snapshot BEFORE any surgery.\n2. Phase 1 per AGENTS.md: rewire main.c → kmain(); Makefile objects;\n   mkpefi shim-only; root-cause loader regression (stale log vs\n   LocateProtocol); gate = KERNEL-OK + out 0x28 + 'E'.\n3. Proceed Phase 2 onward only while gates stay green.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":108,"totalLines":108,"truncated":false}},"title":"home/cyr/kernel/MEMORY.md","time":{"start":1787341831379,"end":1787341831490}},"id":"prt_025dffca9001gQc0J8Zu69LJkz","sessionID":"ses_fda202bcdffec9r6rZINkUTph5","messageID":"msg_025dff51f001z7CIxzjR5UABtv"}}
